 "operation": "pool",
 "distinguishes": "A transaction the canonical modules admit is admitted as they admit it, whatever else the descriptor holds: an unbound ticket the claim-gated rules refuse, and a read of its sender's own unset declared slot beside a relaxed reader. One they refuse for a reason no relaxation answers keeps the canonical code, and one with a dependency is judged under the claims. A pool that runs its alternative modules on canonical transactions fails here.",
